WEBVTT

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.870
Are you okay?

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.950
Can you hear me?

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:19.540
Unidentified male,
appears to be in his mid-thirties,

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.580
What a tragedy.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.700
hit by a truck, unconscious
and in critical condition.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.700
He's done for.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.910
The driver of the truck is unhurt.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.040
Oh, yeah, I was hit by a...

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.660
Two high school students
thought to have also been hit

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.200
are currently missing.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.580
A search is underway.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.040
Requesting immediate backup. Over.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.910
Did those three make it out okay?

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.200
He's heavy! Be careful!

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.660
You bet I am.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.660
I've been a recluse for 20 years.
I just had to bang on the floor for food.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.740
Zenith! Anipa bayhebu! La took!

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.240
Hm?

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.330
Do you know where you are?

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.490
Pipe down. You don't have to shout.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.790
Epabuhia! Akunaja taku! La took!

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.410
Huh? What?

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.290
Blood pressure dropping!

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.580
Prepare a transfusion!

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.830
Can you hear me?

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.580
Do you know your name?

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.790
Can you speak?

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.870
Huh? Am I dying?

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:26.580
Oh, well, my life was basically over anyway.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:31.580
I wish I could've at least lost my virginity.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.200
Epabuhia! Tauwka seio kwa! Pahail za!

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.490
Ivin kav Zenith! Pahail za!

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.620
Ow, my eyes!

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.990
Am I still alive?

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:53.540
Zevaiah bazalfben kifu zivaikah kwav!

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.540
Hey, who's this guy?

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.870
Seriously?

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.990
I'm 100-plus kilos, and he lifted me like...

00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:01.120
Bukay aiha naiboo!

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.200
Whoa! What the hell?!

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.120
Stop! That's gross!

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.410
What the hell? Give me a break.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:06.020
Zenith, tipen, eyuji, tawka paihail kwa.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.410
Whoa.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:08.620
What's she blushing like that for?

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.990
Her tits are huge.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.160
Evun on. Nora iv aihen kap.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.830
What language is that?

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:19.990
Wait, where am I? This isn't a hospital?

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.790
What the hell is he doing?
I'm seriously injured.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.200
Still, she's gorgeous.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.700
Is she European?

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.370
If you leave yourself that open,
I might cop a feel.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.740
Huh?

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.450
It looks like I got reincarnated.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.450
I can't believe something
that crazy happened for real.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:00.410
Paul and Zenith. In their mid-20s, I'd guess.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.290
Moraiha kwa.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.200
Zai.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.950
Tawkah, za iksalaib.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.580
I'm 34, so they're practically kids to me.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.450
Zevaika vawksay Rudy!

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:07.700
I'm seriously jealous of them,
making babies at their age.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.290
Still, getting to suck on
a hottie's tits for free rules.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.790
It didn't turn me on, though.
Maybe 'cause she's my mom?

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.700
Rudy?

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.740
Where are you?

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:21.950
Rudeus?

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.580
I guess my name's "Rudeus."

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.330
After six months, I've got
a pretty good grip on the language.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:33.950
Maybe it's because I'm young,
but I feel like I learn weirdly fast.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.240
Lilia the maid.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.490
She's wonderfully endowed.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.450
Hey, Rudy!

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.240
You shouldn't wander around on your own.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.120
This doesn't go on your head.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.910
What's wrong, Lilia?

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:05.700
Lady Zenith, this is
a little difficult to say, but...

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.040
Well...

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.660
...perhaps Master Rudeus is afflicted by some...

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.200
Oh, no. It's nothing.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.830
What are you being evasive for?

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:16.950
He's a child.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.540
He doesn't know any better.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.540
No.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.200
What a view.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.200
I've seen photos like this.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.410
Is this Europe, like I thought?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.120
Still,

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.830
Do you think this is enough?

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.120
it's definitely <i>way</i> too rural.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:39.830
Yes.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.790
You handle that, then, Lilia.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.330
No electricity or gas? What year is it?

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.330
Of course.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.290
I might be reborn, but I still
want to play with a computer.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.490
Hey, what?

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.410
What's he doing?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.330
Oh crap.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.080
Rudy?!

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.160
Rudy!

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.540
Young Master!

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.990
Is he all right?

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:15.490
You're not supposed to move
people who've hit their heads, lady.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.660
Even after that, he isn't crying.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.540
There, there.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.490
Just in case,

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:26.950
I'll do a spell to make the pain go away.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.700
Divine power is rich and nourishing.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.660
Hey, are you kidding me?

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.700
This is this country's
version of kissing a boo boo?

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.200
to those who have lost their strength.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.200
Are both my parents delusional nerds?

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.490
Did the fighter marry the cleric?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.740
Healing.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.290
Well? It doesn't hurt anymore, right?

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:08.370
You wouldn't know it,
but Mommy used to be an adventurer.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.290
What is it?

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:10.410
I heard a loud--

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.080
Dear! Rudy fell on his head and...!

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.290
Calm down. He's a kid.
Of course he'll fall down sometimes.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.620
Besides, if he gets hurt,
you can just heal him.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.620
Don't tell me I'm in...

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.160
But what if he gets hurt
so badly that I can't heal him?

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.450
It'll be fine.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.580
Actually, this pretty much confirms it.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.120
This isn't Earth. It's another world.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:35.990
A world of sword and sorcery.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.490
I'm steady on my feet now.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.200
Still, magic, huh?

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.870
Magic...

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.120
That's a word that'd get even a monkey excited.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.700
I want to try it out myself ASAP.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.790
That said, there's not much I can do right now.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.080
Books?

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.200
There are only five books in the house.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.990
Either books are expensive in this world,
or Paul and Zenith aren't big readers.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:43.160
I used to have nearly a thousand,
so it's hard to believe.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.240
All light novels, though.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.450
I can't read it. I'll have
to learn to read first.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:53.990
About another year passed.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:58.660
Even with just five books, with the
help of Paul reading to me sometimes,

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.370
I can more-or-less read now.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:08.120
Although I do wonder if he expects
a baby to understand what's in these books.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.620
Still, this book is fascinating.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.200
<i>The Magic Manual</i> .

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.790
I've seen some of this stuff in my old life.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:19.870
Like, there are two ways to activate magic:
incantations and magic circles,

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:23.370
but incantations dominate
the mainstream right now, etc.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.620
There's a lot of background.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.620
But I'm more concerned that, according to this,

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.990
your magic power is
basically set-in-stone at birth.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.200
I'm worried.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.410
I doubt my genes are going to put in much work.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:39.740
Well, I guess I'll give it a shot.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:49.540
Umm... "Let the great protection
of water be on the place thou seekest.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.410
I call a refreshing,
burbling stream here and now.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.660
Water Ball."

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.290
Shouldn't it go flying?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.080
One more try.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:26.870
It's like practicing combos in a fighter.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:30.740
Concentrate, picture it over
and over in your head,

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.200
then actually do it.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.290
Huh?

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.410
I didn't do the incantation yet.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.040
What gives?

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.620
Huh?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.580
This is all the MP I've got?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.490
Honestly, Rudy.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:12.450
If you're sleepy, you should go
to the bathroom and then to bed.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:13.740
Damn it.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:16.660
I'm too old to look like I wet myself!

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:19.410
Damn it. Damn it.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.120
Huh?

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.540
I experimented for a while and learned a lot.

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:37.240
This book's full of it!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:40.410
Magic power grows the more you use it,

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.660
and magic works without incantations.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.120
I guess I can't believe everything I read.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:51.370
But if it's this easy,
what's even the point of incantations?

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:59.200
Maybe incantations are
a system for automating magic.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.660
Holy Millis who watches
over us in distant lands,

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:01.240
we thank you for blessing us
with life-giving nourishment.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:04.120
They do it all for you without
the need to focus on every single spell.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:04.120
Time to eat!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.450
If so, there's a big advantage to them.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.410
First, they're easy to teach.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.620
An incantation is all you need to cast,

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.330
so as magic was taught,

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:18.450
maybe over time people started
to think incantations were necessary.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.160
Second, convenience.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.040
Attack magic is probably used in combat,

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:29.740
Thus, Perugius led his
12 followers to the Devil Laplace.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:29.740
and saying an incantation fast would
be quicker than closing your eyes to focus.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.490
I think it's your bedtime now, Rudy.

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.580
Dear, I can't take any more!

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:38.740
I'm just getting started.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.740
My growing magic power is another mystery.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:45.870
Could it be the result of my training?

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:49.660
There's supposed to be a cap on
magic power, even if you work at it.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:52.540
No, it's too soon to draw conclusions.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.490
Yes. It could increase
as I grow up, for example.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:01.950
Or maybe using magic at an early age
dramatically increases my maximum.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.330
Oh,

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:07.160
I shouldn't discount the
possibility that I'm unique.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.450
I've gotten into this!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.160
Whoops. That's no good. Cool it.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:15.370
If that hypothesis is right,
there's only one thing to do:

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:19.410
Train as much as I can while I'm still growing.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.910
Okay!

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:25.740
Still, how do I make these fly?

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.200
What?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.240
Yes! All right!

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.160
I finally cracked how this incantation works.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:02.740
This spell goes: create, set size,
set firing speed, activate.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.240
That's the process it follows.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.910
At least, I'm pretty sure that's it.

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:12.080
I didn't set the firing speed,
so it didn't go anywhere.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:22.040
I've got more magic power now,
so it's time I tried intermediate magic.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.240
Umm...

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:31.660
"Supple spirit of water and princess
of streams that flow through the earth,

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:36.120
sweep away all things
with your hidden inner might.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.410
Splash Flow."

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.200
What happened?!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.120
H-Hey!

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:07.080
What's going on?

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.950
Rudy?!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:09.990
Rudy!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:10.950
Are you hurt?!

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.410
N-No.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.370
Was it a monster?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.660
No, around here there aren't...

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.240
Oh?

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:27.490
Rudy, did you read this book out loud?

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:28.620
Huh? Scary.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.040
What's that look?

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:35.040
Maybe kids who use magic are dangerous
and get sent off to an inquisition?

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.620
No! I don't want to get burned!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:42.950
I'm sorry.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.330
Did you hear that, dear?!

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.700
I knew our boy was a genius!

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.080
Hang on. This is an intermediate--

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.370
Let's hire a magic tutor right now!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.410
But wait, we haven't even taught him to re--

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.910
I'm sure he'll grow up to be an amazing mage!

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.870
Wait a minute! We promised that
if it were a boy, he'd be a swordsman.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.950
But he can do intermediate magic at his age!

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.450
A promise is a promise!

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:09.370
You're one to talk!
You break yours all the time!

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.290
This has nothing to do with me!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:17.910
Why not teach him magic in the morning
and swordsmanship in the afternoon?

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:21.160
It's not good to fight
in front of the baby, dear.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:23.370
I guess not.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.790
And so, we decided to hire me a magic tutor.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.540
He spends all day at home swinging his sword,

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:32.790
but Paul's technically a knight
put in charge of this village.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:37.490
I guess that's why he can
afford a tutor for a kid like me.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.200
But this is the sticks on
the edge of the country.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.450
Will anyone actually apply out here?

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:47.540
Or so I worried, but they found one in no time.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:52.490
My parents expected
a retired adventurer to apply.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.080
Good day.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:52.490
Good day.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:57.490
So, we figured on a middle-aged
or old man with a big, bushy beard,

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.390
Good day.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:01.540
a veteran spellcaster who really screams "mage."

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.450
I'm Roxy Migurdia.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.410
Pleased to meet you.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.200
What the hell?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:12.740
Forget a beard; she looks like
her bush hasn't grown in yet.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.040
Maybe middle-school age?

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:17.620
Loli, scornful gaze, unsociable:
three traits that equal perfection.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.080
I want to marry her.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.290
Oh, you're the, um... home tutor?

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.830
You're awfully, well...

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.620
She's tiny!

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:28.290
You're a fine one to talk.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.990
Maybe she's sensitive about it?

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.410
I didn't mean her chest, though.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.620
So, where is the student I'll be teaching?

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.160
Oh, he's right here!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.450
You do see them sometimes.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.910
Idiot parents who think their kid has
talent just because he's an early bloomer.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:49.450
We can hear you, Roxy!

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.450
Looks like this one's a dud.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.080
Excuse me?

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:52.080
Nothing!

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:56.830
Only, I doubt that child could
comprehend the theory of magic.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:01.490
Don't worry! Our little Rudy is amazing!

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:06.700
I understand. I'll do what I can.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.620
Huh? We're doing it outside?

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.370
Naturally.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:20.830
In broad terms, there are
only three types of magic.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:24.370
Attack magic, healing magic,
and summoning magic.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:27.540
Each is divided into seven ranks:

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:33.200
beginner, intermediate, advanced,
sacred, royal, imperial, and divine.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:36.700
And to use magic, you need magical power.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:40.120
Either the magical power within you, or...

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.450
Is something wrong?

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.580
Oh, no.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.790
All right, then.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:49.870
Anyway, I'll start by demonstrating
an incantation, so repeat after me.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:53.160
Do you need the incantation?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.950
Of course you do.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:57.160
I thought so.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:03.370
Let the great protection of water
be on the place thou seekest.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:06.290
I call a refreshing,
burbling stream here and now.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:08.330
Water Ball!

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.870
What do you think?

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:20.620
Miss, my mom worked hard to raise
that tree, so I think she'll get mad.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:21.700
Huh?

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.240
Th-That won't do, will it?

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:28.160
Divine power is rich and nourishing.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:32.740
It offers the strength to rise again
to those who have lost their strength.

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.330
Healing!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.830
Oh, wow.

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:40.240
You can use healing magic, too!

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:42.040
Yes, up to intermediate level.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.160
Wow! That's amazing!

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:49.120
No, anyone can do as much
if they train properly.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.830
She seems like a pushover.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.490
Now, you try it.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:54.870
Okay!

00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.450
The Magic Manual didn't mention
incantation-less spells either.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:05.040
I'd been using them without thinking,
but maybe that's taboo.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.620
Roxy said you need incantations, too,

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.240
so I should say them for now.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:12.450
They could be important.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:16.910
Let the great protection of water
be on the place thou seekest...

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:22.910
What are you doing?

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.740
Oh, n-nothing!

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:26.200
How did I do?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.870
You cut the incantation short.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:30.830
I did.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.450
Do you always abridge it like that?

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:36.490
I usually... just skip it.

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:38.870
Completely?!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:42.790
So, you usually omit the incantation.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:44.830
I see.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:48.040
It looks like you'll be worth training.

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.620
Oh.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:01.620
Roxy! Don't use my trees as test subjects!

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:02.160
Huh?

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.450
Oh, honestly!

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:09.540
I screwed up right away.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.740
I guess I'll be fired tomorrow.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:15.700
I'm sorry, miss. It was my fault.

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:20.040
Damn it. I hadn't had a
conversation in almost 20 years.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:23.490
I don't know what to say at times like this.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.950
No, think. You've done this lots of times.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:30.290
What would a dating sim
protagonist do in this situation?

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:38.370
You didn't screw up, miss,
you gained experience.

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:43.870
I-I suppose so.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.160
Thank you very much.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.870
Ow!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.040
More importantly, Roxy.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.040
Y-Yes!

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:00.830
Let's go inside.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:04.290
Let's start by introducing ourselves, okay?

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.450
Hey!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.660
Hurry up!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:16.620
I'm grateful, but I have
nothing to offer you in return.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:17.990
Don't be silly.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.160
Now, come on in.

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:24.080
You, too, Rudy.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.870
Okay!

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:37.990
Okay, let's get Roxy's welcome party started!

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.330
It's like a dream.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:43.040
A dream I'm having as I die from that crash.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:43.950
No.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:46.540
Even if it is, I don't care.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:50.410
In this world, I bet even I can make it.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:53.120
If I live and try as hard as everyone else,

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:57.620
get back up when I fall,
and keep facing forward,

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.490
then maybe I can do it.

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:01.450
Maybe even I...

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:04.490
Maybe even a jobless, reclusive bum like me

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:07.240
can get a do-over at life...

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:12.010
Episode 1

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:12.010
Jobless Reincarnation

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:12.040
...and can get serious about living.

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:42.040
"Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation"

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:47.030
Next time

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:47.030
Teacher
